From 9760f3ae9560573285e14372c1c323d1ea61fdea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chedy Souffargi <cs@karo-electronics.de>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:20:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: ddr: wait for self-refresh entry as ERR052794
 requires

DDR_EnterRetention() implements the software self-refresh entry of
ERR052794 (IMX95_P21N Rev.2, p.17-18). Step 4 of the workaround reads:
"Wait for either 8000 DRAM CK cycles or DEBUG_2[3] to be set. DEBUG_2 is
at DDRC register offset of 0xf04."

The code polled bit 2 instead of bit 3, and with the polarity reversed:
it spun while the bit was set and left as soon as it was clear. Since the
entry is forced with FRC_SR, the loop returned immediately and the
retention sequence carried on before the DRAM was in self refresh, which
is the spec violation the erratum describes. The 8000 CK alternative was
not implemented either.

Poll DEBUG_2[3] until it is set, bounded by exactly 8000 DRAM clock
cycles measured on the 24 MHz system counter (4.3 us at 3733 MT/s). A
longer bound must not be used: a 25 us wait was tried and the board no
longer resumed from suspend, consistent with the DDRC leaving self
refresh on its own in that window, which is the very defect described.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/ddr/fsl_ddr.c | 17 ++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ddr/fsl_ddr.c b/drivers/ddr/fsl_ddr.c
index c855e02..8379623 100644
--- a/drivers/ddr/fsl_ddr.c
+++ b/drivers/ddr/fsl_ddr.c
@@ -226,14 +226,17 @@ bool DDR_EnterRetention(const struct ddr_info *ddrp)
                 DDRC->DDR_SDRAM_CFG_2 |=
                     (1UL << DDRC_DDR_SDRAM_CFG_2_FRC_SR_SHIFT);
 
-                /* ERR052794:
-                 * Step 3: Enter self refresh, previously performed above
-                 * Step 4: Wait DEBUG_2[3] (SR) to be set
-                 *         If SR=1: Memory controller is in self refresh
-                 */
-                while ((Read32(DEBUG_2) & 0x4U) != 0U)
+                /* ERR052794 step 4: DEBUG_2[3] SR set or 8000 CK (IMX95_P21N p.18) */
                 {
-                    ; /* Intentional empty while */
+                    /* 8000 CK in 24 MHz SYSCTR ticks, CK = MT/s / 2 */
+                    uint32_t ticks = (8000U * 48U) / ddrp->pstate_freq[0U];
+                    uint32_t t0 = SYSCTR_GetCounter32();
+
+                    while (((Read32(DEBUG_2) & 0x8U) == 0U)
+                        && ((SYSCTR_GetCounter32() - t0) < ticks))
+                    {
+                        ; /* Intentional empty while */
+                    }
                 }
 
                 /* Clear PHY INIT complete: BIT2 PHY_INIT_CMPLT W1C */
